{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "102", "sample_idx": 8, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "\"Oh, darling, you look… comfortable,\" Seraphina said, fluttering her eyelashes as she surveyed Leo in his well-worn sweatpants and oversized hoodie. Her ball gown, a shimmering emerald green, flowed around her like liquid moonlight.\n\nLeo shrugged, pulling the hoodie tighter. \"And you look like you're about to float away. Are you *sure* about this, Sera? It's just the Tuesday Night Trivia at O'Malley's.\"\n\nSeraphina gasped dramatically. \"Just trivia? Leo, darling, it’s *O'Malley's* trivia! They have themed nights! Tonight is 'Decades' – think roaring twenties, groovy seventies, and… well, whatever decade inspires you!\" She twirled, the gown swirling with her.\n\n\"Right,\" Leo mumbled, adjusting his glasses. \"Decades. I was thinking more along the lines of 'comfort and minimal effort.'\"\n\n\"Honestly! You never embrace an opportunity for glamour! I've been planning my ensemble for a week. This gown is vintage, you know. It belonged to my great-aunt Mildred!\"\n\n\"Mildred sounds… fabulous.\" Leo offered a weak smile. \"Look, I appreciate the invitation. I just… I’m not really a ball gown kind of guy.\"\n\nSeraphina sighed, a hint of exasperation in her voice. \"Alright, alright. No need to be difficult. But at least *try* to look presentable. No bare feet, please.\"\n\n\"Deal. No bare feet. Is there, like, a dress code I missed?\"\n\n\"Just… be yourself, but a slightly more presentable version of yourself. And try to answer at least one trivia question correctly!\" She patted his arm. \"Now, come on! We’re going to be late!\"\n\n*   Leo sighed again, resigned to his fate. He knew arguing with Seraphina was a losing battle.\n*   Seraphina adjusted the train of her gown, ensuring it didn’t drag on the floor as they headed out.\n*   He muttered under his breath, \"Decades. I should have just stayed home and watched documentaries about the 1950s.\"\n\